# Line endings are stored as LF in the repository and restored as CRLF on checkout, on every
# machine and on the CI runner alike.
#
# This is not cosmetic. build/Build-SingleFile.ps1 rejects any source part whose lines end in
# a bare LF, and tests/StaticChecks.ps1 asserts the same for the assembled script, because the
# shipped file has always used CRLF. Without this file the result would depend on whatever
# core.autocrlf happens to be set to locally or on the runner, so an identical commit could
# build on one machine and fail on another.
* text=auto eol=crlf

# Checksums are consumed by tooling that expects exactly the bytes the release workflow wrote.
*.sha256 -text
